Hogwarts legacy's character creator has  been fully revealed including that  mysterious final tab that had only been  teased thus far of course we've gotten  bits and pieces along the way regarding  the Character Creator but it wasn't  until the recent gameplay showcase that  Avalanche fully revealed the Character  Creator options with the help of expecto  go our favorite Merlin conspiracy  theorist Avalanche gave us a detailed  walkthrough of how the Character Creator  will work in the first tab we have a  look at presets and these appear to be  randomly generated presets using various  hairstyles and skin tones as well as two  clothing options this is where you'll  start and I really like this approach  because some players really just want to  get into the game as quickly as possible  and not fine-tune every single detail so  the presets give you that option now I  know for a lot of you listening to this  your jaw may be on the floor that's kind  of hard to believe what they don't want  to customize every single detail some  people don't you know they just want to  jump right in now if you want to really  get into the further customization  options and I assume most of you  watching this video want to do exactly  that then the preset will simply serve  as your Baseline so you can simply  please select one of the options that  are in the ballpark of what you're going  for then you move to the next tab which  is the faceware tab it's here you can  set the face shape skin color and  whether or not you want glasses under  the face shape category we have 15  different options to choose from and  these appear to adjust features like  your nose cheekbones forehead etc for me  I actually think this is a good amount  of control without being overwhelming  now if you're a big gamer and you play a  lot of games in this genre then you are  probably used to having a lot more  control over things like the nose the  chin the cheekbones even the ears I  think here it's pretty clear the team at  Avalanche wanted to go with something a  little bit easier to digest with a focus  on not overwhelming the player but still  trying to give us plenty of variation on  our character then we move to skin color  and there are 20 different options here  which you select by moving the  horizontal slider back and forth after  that you have the option of giving your  character glasses and we start with the  circular spectacles for that Harry  Potter look then we have the half moon  spectacles for a more Dumbledore style  look and then a third option which is  kind of like a hexagon style of glasses  now if this doesn't seem like a lot of  options when it comes to the glasses  don't worry because game director Alan 2  mentioned that through the course of the  game there's a lot of other options  you'll keep unlocking remember all those  shops and hogsmead I'm guessing that's  where we're gonna be able to find some  of those it's also worth noting that  Alan was asked near the end of the  Showcase about what you can or can't  change about the character once you've  started the game so according to him  details like the accessories the glasses  as well as the hair can change looks  like we're gonna have a barber shop in  hogsmead but it sounds like the main  character features like the face shape  and skin tone cannot be changed moving  on to the next page and what I think is  the star of the show in this character  creator the hairstyles you'll start by  picking the hair color at the top and  there are 32 total options then you move  down to the actual hairstyles themselves  and I tried to look through the menu  here and count them all I believe there  are 47 different options and most of  these are just stunning the texture in  the hair just has this level of detail  realism particularly for people of color  that you just don't see in most games  trust me I see all of your comments  about this and I know the team at  Avalanche has seen this as well I think  it's just really impressive what they've  done here and I know it was an important  Focus for the team that worked on the  Character Creator on the next tab we  have complexion and it's here you'll be  able to adjust the complexion as well as  freckles moles and then scars and  markings the complexion was a little bit  interesting since we already had skin  tones but it appears to be a more subtle  adjustment to the skin giving you the  option to darken the eyes a little bit  or shade the cheeks it appears there are  nine options for that category looks  like 10 options in the middle here for  freckles and moles and then we have nine  options for scars and markings with the  first option here just being no scars or  markings at all the next tab is all  about the eyes and we'll have  adjustments for eye color eyebrow color  and then eyebrow shape I counted 25  options on the eye color 33 for eyebrows  and then we have 20 options for eyebrow  shape including the very last one here  which appears to be no eyebrows at all  and then we move to the final tab which  to this point has been a complete  mystery the main title of this tab is  finalize your character and it's here  you'll choose between two tones of voice  and then be able to adjust the pitch of  your character's voice we officially  have four confirmed difficulty options  with your usual easy normal and hard  difficulties but also a story option  which is actually a step below easy this  is intended for those Potter fans or  anyone playing Hogwarts Legacy who  aren't usually Gamers but still want to  play this game because of being able to  go back to Hogwarts as our very own  witch or wizard we also get to see brief  definitions for each one starting with  story which is said to be a focus on  story with minimal gameplay challenge  easy if you play on easy you'll get a  light gameplay challenge normal a  balanced gameplay Challenge and finally  hard a demanding gameplay challenge  after setting the difficulty you'll get  to name your character that's right  first and last name this is a big one  that puts to rest some of the  speculation we had as fans about whether  or not we'd be a witch or wizard from a  specific family this would also seem to  rule out anyone calling us out by our  name in the game and to be fair I know  it's possible there are some games  before particularly sports games who  have actually programmed a number of  names into the game but I would not  expect that here for Hogwarts Legacy and  and finally you'll choose whether you  want to be a witch or Wizard and this is  the choice that will determine your  player character's dormitory from there  you'll be off to Hogwarts to experience  an original story from The Wizarding  World set in the late 1800s if you want  to get caught up on everything we know  about the lore and Story So Far check  out that video on the right side of your  screen now as always thank you all so  much for watching I'll talk to you again  soon
 

